
%9Syntax:%9

@SYNTAX:network@

%9Description:%9

    IRCNET is the same command as NETWORK, kept for compatibility with older
    versions. It takes the same subcommands (LIST, ADD, MODIFY and REMOVE)
    and options; replace NETWORK with IRCNET in the syntax above. Without a
    parameter, the list of networks is displayed.

    See /HELP NETWORK for the description of the parameters.

%9Examples:%9

    /IRCNET
    /IRCNET ADD -nick alice -usermode +i ExampleNet
    /IRCNET REMOVE ExampleNet

%9See also:%9 NETWORK, SERVER

